## 7. NETWORKING & VPN ROUTING

Security is enforced by blocking all inbound WAN traffic. Tailscale acts as a Virtual LAN gateway, assigning a secure tailnet IP address to the node.

Traefik handles TLS routing using a dual approach:
1. **Tailscale SSL Certs**: Retrieves certificates from the Tailscale API for single-device tailnet domains (e.g., Actual Budget).
2. **acme-dns Wildcard Certs**: Solves DNS-01 challenges via **acme-dns.io** to provision a wildcard certificate (`*.local.surjyadipsen.in`), bypassing domain-wide HSTS policies for self-hosted apps (e.g., Booklore).

{% accordion %}
{% accordionItem title="Routing Logic Diagram" %}
{% mermaid
   code="flowchart TD\n    Request([Client Request]) --> NetCheck{Client Location?}\n    NetCheck -->|Local LAN| HotspotAP[Connect to Pi 5 Hotspot AP]\n    NetCheck -->|Outside LAN| Tailnet[Establish encrypted Tailnet tunnel]\n\n    HotspotAP --> RouteLocal[Direct access via AP Wi-Fi]\n    Tailnet --> RouteTS[VPN interface tunnel]\n\n    RouteLocal --> Traefik[Traefik Ingress Router]\n    RouteTS --> Traefik\n\n    Traefik --> DynamicRouting{Traefik Label Matching}\n    DynamicRouting -->|actual.domain| AB[Actual Budget Stack]\n    DynamicRouting -->|immich.domain| IM[Immich Stack]\n    DynamicRouting -->|paperless.domain| PL[Paperless-ngx Stack]\n    DynamicRouting -->|resume.domain| RR[Reactive Resume Stack]\n    DynamicRouting -->|booklore.domain| BL[Booklore Stack]" /%}
{% /accordionItem %}
{% /accordion %}

